{# The Huntsville Gutter Problem #}
<section class="problem-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-content">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">The Local Challenge</p>
        <h2>Why Huntsville Gutters Need Regular Cleaning</h2>
        
        <p>Here's the thing about North Alabama: we've got the perfect combination of conditions to clog gutters fast. Pine trees dropping needles year-round. Oak trees releasing those helicopter seeds in spring and dumping leaves in fall. And when it rains here, it doesn't drizzle—those afternoon thunderstorms drop two inches in twenty minutes.</p>
        
        <p>When debris piles up in your gutters, water has nowhere to go. It spills over the edge, runs down your fascia boards, and pools around your foundation. And the red clay soil around here doesn't absorb that water—it just sits there, pushing against your foundation walls. Over time, you get cracks, settling, and water in the basement.</p>
        
        <p>We've seen it hundreds of times. A homeowner ignores the gutters for a few seasons, and suddenly they're looking at foundation repairs that cost ten times what regular gutter cleaning would have. The gutters are the first line of defense—they just need to be clear to do their job.</p>
      </div>
