{# Signs You Need Cleaning #}
<section class="process-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Warning Signs</p>
      <h2>How to Know Your Gutters Need Cleaning</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Not sure if it's time? Here's what to look for:</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="process-steps">
      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-number">1</div>
        <h3>Water Overflowing During Rain</h3>
        <p>If water pours over the gutter edge during rainstorms instead of flowing to the downspouts, you've got a clog somewhere. This is the most obvious sign.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-number">2</div>
        <h3>Plants Growing in Gutters</h3>
        <p>If you can see weeds, grass, or even small trees sprouting from your gutters, there's enough accumulated debris to support plant life. That's a serious clog.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-number">3</div>
        <h3>Staining on Fascia Boards</h3>
        <p>Dark streaks or water stains on the boards behind your gutters mean water has been spilling over and running down the wood. This leads to rot if not addressed.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-number">4</div>
        <h3>Sagging Gutters</h3>
        <p>Gutters that sag or pull away from the house are often weighed down by debris and standing water. The extra weight strains the hangers and fascia.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-number">5</div>
        <h3>Birds or Pests Nesting</h3>
        <p>Birds love building nests in clogged gutters—all that debris makes perfect nesting material. If you see bird activity around your roofline, check your gutters.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="process-step">
        <div class="step-number">6</div>
        <h3>It's Been More Than 6 Months</h3>
        <p>Even if everything looks fine from the ground, gutters accumulate debris you can't see. If it's been more than six months since your last cleaning, it's time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

